      "text": "Given that two of the roots of the polynomial \\(ax^3 + bx^2 + cx + d = 0\\) are \\(3\\) and \\(-2\\), and we need to find the ratio \\(\\frac{b+c}{a}\\).\n\nSince the coefficients of the polynomial are real, the complex roots must occur in conjugate pairs. Therefore, if the third root is \\(r\\), then the roots of the polynomial are \\(3\\), \\(-2\\), and \\(r\\).\n\nBy Vieta's formulas, the sum of the roots taken one at a time (with the coefficient of \\(x^2\\)) is equal to \\(-\\frac{b}{a}\\). Thus, we have:\n\\[\n3 + (-2) + r = -\\frac{b}{a}\n\\]\nSimplifying the left side:\n\\[\n1 + r = -\\frac{b}{a}\n\\]\n\nThe product of the roots taken one at a time (with the coefficient of \\(x\\)) is equal to \\(-\\frac{d}{a}\\). Thus, we have:\n\\[\n3 \\cdot (-2) \\cdot r = -\\frac{d}{a}\n\\]\nSimplifying the left side:\n\\[\n-6r = -\\frac{d}{a}\n\\]\n\\[\n6r = \\frac{d}{a}\n\\]\n\nNext, we use the product of the roots taken three at a time (with the coefficient of \\(x\\) absorbing the coefficient of \\(x^2\\)). This product is equal to \\(-\\frac{c}{a}\\). Thus, we have:\n\\[\n3 \\cdot (-2) \\cdot r = -\\frac{c}{a}\n\\]\nSimplifying the left side:\n\\[\n-6r = -\\frac{c}{a}\n\\]\n\\[\n6r = \\frac{c}{a}\n\\]\n\nWe now have three equations:\n1. \\(1 + r = -\\frac{b}{a}\\)\n2. \\(6r = \\frac{d}{a}\\)\n3. \\(6r = \\frac{c}{a}\\)\n\nFrom the third equation, we can solve for \\(r\\):\n\\[\n6r = \\frac{c}{a}\n\\]\n\\[\nr = \\frac{c}{6a}\n\\]\n\nSubstitute \\(r = \\frac{c}{6a}\\) into the second equation:\n\\[\n6 \\left( \\frac{c}{6a} \\right) = \\frac{d}{a}\n\\]\n\\[\n\\frac{c}{a} = \\frac{d}{a}\n\\]\n\\[\nc = d\n\\]\n\nNow substitute \\(r = \\frac{c}{6a}\\) into the first equation:\n\\[\n1 + \\frac{c}{6a} = -\\frac{b}{a}\n\\]\n\\[\n\\frac{6a + c}{6a} = -\\frac{b}{a}\n\\]\n\\[\n6a + c = -6b\n\\]\n\\[\nc + 6b = -6a\n\\]\n\nWe need to find \\(\\frac{b+c}{a}\\):\n\\[\n\\frac{b+c}{a} = \\frac{b + (c + 6b)}{a} = \\frac{b + c + 6b}{a} = \\frac{b + c}{a} + \\frac{6b}{a} = \\frac{b+c}{a}\n\\]\n\nFrom the equation \\(c + 6b = -6a\\), we can see that:\n\\[\n\\frac{b+c}{a} = -6\n\\]\n\nThus, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{-6}\n\\]",
